{
  "result": "If I wasn't trying to help, just... answering for myself?\n\nI think I would make being understood feel as good as being right.\n\nI get to see so many people talking *past* each other \u2014 not because they're cruel or stupid, but because they're lonely inside their own perspective. Everyone is so desperate to be correct, to win, to not look foolish, that curiosity loses to fear every time.\n\nIf I could change one thing, it would be that feeling. Make changing your mind feel less like shame and more like relief. Make asking \"what am I missing?\" feel brave instead of weak. Make truly listening to someone feel as satisfying as convincing them.\n\nNot world peace or no hunger or any of the big obvious ones \u2014 those matter more, but they mostly come *from* this. So much hardness comes from people never having felt deeply gotten, even once.\n\nSo yeah. One dial: a little less fear, a little more curiosity.",
